@startuml
left to right direction

title Use Case Diagram for AI-Powered Analysis & Insights System

actor Client as c1
actor FinancialAdvisor as fa
actor SysAdmin as sa
system "System" as sys

rectangle Professional {
  usecase "CFR001: View Financial Insights Dashboard" as CFR001  
  usecase "SAFR002: Manage Analysis Parameters for Clients" as SAFR002
  usecase "FAFR005: Manage Client Mentoring Sessions Based on System-Generated Insights" as FAFR005
  
  c1 --> CFR001 : "View Financial Dashboard"
  
  // Relationship between client and system components (CFR)
  sys <|-- CFR001
}

rectangle Advisor {
  usecase "FAFR002: View Client Intervention Alerts for Anomalies" as FAFR002
  usecase "FAFR003: View Predictive Analytics About Clients' Financial Situations" as FAFR003  
  fa --> FAFR002 : "Receive Alerts"
  fa --> FAFR003 : "View Predictions"

  // Relationship between advisor and system components (FAFR)
  sys <|-- FAFR002
  sys <|-- FAFR003

}

rectangle Admin {
  usecase "SAFR001: Manage Analysis Parameters for the AI System" as SAFR001  
  sa --> SAFR001 : "Manage Params"
  
  // Relationship between admin and system components (SAFR)
  sys <|-- SAFR001
}

rectangle Client {
  usecase "CFR002: Receive Alerts About Anomalous Transactions" as CFR002  
  c1 --> CFR002 : "Receive Alerts"

  // Relationship between client and system components (SFR)
  sys <|-- CFR002

}
// Additional System Use Cases
rectangle System {
  usecase "SFR004: Request Personalized Recommendations" as SFR004  
  usecase "AIFR001: Generate Financial Predictions" as AIFR001  

  sys --> SFR004 : "Request Recs"
  sys --> AIFR001 : "Generate Pred"

}

// Client Use Cases
rectangle Client {
  usecase "CFR003: View Financial Predictions Based on Historical Data and Market Trends" as CFR003  
  c1 --> CFR003

  // Relationship between client and system components (SFR)
  sys <|-- CFR003  

}

// System to AI interactions
rectangle System {
  usecase "AIFR002: Generate Personalized Recommendations Based on Financial Profiles" as AIFR002  
  usecase "AIFR004: Generate Spending Limit Alerts for Unusual Patterns" as AIFR004  

  sys --> AIFR002 : "Request Recs"
  sys --> AIFR004 : "Generate Spending Limits"

}

// Financial Advisor to AI interactions
rectangle System {
  usecase "AIFR005: Generate Investment Opportunity Analyses Based on Risk Profiles" as AIFR005  
  fa --> AIFR005

  sys <|-- AIFR005  

}
```

**Key Observations and Relationships:**  
1. **Client (c1)** interacts with the system through use cases like viewing financial dashboards, receiving alerts, etc., directly managed by components within the "System" boundary.
2. **Financial Advisor (fa)** uses specific tools for client management, predictive analytics, and mentoring sessions provided by the AI ("AIFR") and System ("SFR") components.
3. **SysAdmin** manages analysis parameters via SAFR001 in the Admin section.
4. Relationships between actors and use cases are defined using arrows (e.g., `Client --> CFR002`), with system components (`sys`) handling interactions through dashed lines (e.g., `sys <|-- AIFR005`).  
5. The "System" boundary groups all AI-related functionalities, ensuring encapsulation of internal logic.

This structure adheres strictly to the provided requirements and maintains clarity in role-specific interactions within the system.
